# Schema gate exemptions (P1211) — read by scripts/check-schema-ready.sh.
#
# The gate refuses to let a SHA become origin/main while any migration file in its
# tree is missing from prod's supabase_migrations.schema_migrations, and it requires
# exactly one file per version. This file lists the only exceptions.
#
# The gate reads this file from the TRUSTED ref (origin/main), never from the commit
# being checked: an entry added in a push takes effect only after that push has
# landed, so a push can never exempt its own migration.
#
# Format — one entry per line, a reason is mandatory:
#   legacy   <basename>                : <reason>
#   dup-pair <basename> <basename>     : <reason>
#
# legacy   — a file the runner never applies (no version prefix). Exempt from the
#            ledger check entirely.
# dup-pair — a grandfathered P1042 collision. Both files share one version; the pair
#            is allowed ONLY with exactly these two members. A third file on that
#            version fails the gate (exit 2), which is the hole the existing
#            duplicate check has: it skips allowlisted versions wholesale.
#
# No regexes, no wildcards: a new exemption must be a visible, reviewed diff.

legacy p63_google_oauth_avatar.sql : no version prefix, so migrate.sh skips it; pre-dates the ledger (P63)

